// XFAIL: RT-165: a static holding a raw pointer (`*const i64`, a struct of a `*mut i64`, an array of `*mut u8`) is accepted; rustc refuses each (E0277, not Sync) (0.30.2)
// rustc: three E0277 `*const i64` / `*mut i64` / `*mut u8` "cannot be shared
// between threads safely" at lines 17, 18, 19 (twin:
// r302d_011_static_raw_pointer_accepted.rs.txt). vole builds it and prints
// `true true true`: front/threads.vl check_static_cells skips every Freeze type
// ("Rust's whole rule, that every immutable static is Sync, is 0.27's"); a raw
// pointer is Freeze and not Sync. No memory error from safe code (a deref needs
// unsafe), but a pointer in a static is shared by every thread unvouched.
// Since v0.28.0.
// ERROR: Sync
// ERROR: line 17
// ERROR-COUNT: 3
struct P {
    p: *mut i64,
}

static A: *const i64 = 0 as *const i64;
static B: P = P { p: 0 as *mut i64 };
static C: [*mut u8; 2] = [0 as *mut u8, 0 as *mut u8];

fn main() {
    println("{} {} {}", A.is_null(), B.p.is_null(), C[1].is_null());
}
